# MATLAB Program: Ultrasound Signal Conversion (Voltage vs Time) to (Magnitude dB vs Frequency MHz)

## Basic Version

```matlab
%% Ultrasound Signal Analysis: Time Domain to Frequency Domain
% Converts voltage vs time to magnitude (dB) vs frequency (MHz)

clear; clc; close all;

%% ============== USER PARAMETERS ==============
% Sampling parameters
Fs = 100e6;          % Sampling frequency (Hz) - 100 MHz
duration = 50e-6;    % Signal duration (seconds) - 50 microseconds

% Ultrasound signal parameters (for demonstration)
f_center = 5e6;      % Center frequency (Hz) - 5 MHz typical ultrasound
bandwidth = 2e6;     % Bandwidth (Hz)

%% ============== GENERATE SAMPLE SIGNAL ==============
% Time vector
t = 0:1/Fs:duration-1/Fs;
N = length(t);       % Number of samples

% Create sample ultrasound pulse (Gaussian-modulated sinusoid)
% Replace this section with your actual data import
envelope = exp(-((t - duration/2).^2) / (2*(duration/10)^2));
voltage_signal = envelope .* sin(2*pi*f_center*t);

% Add some noise (optional)
voltage_signal = voltage_signal + 0.05*randn(size(voltage_signal));

%% ============== FFT COMPUTATION ==============
% Compute FFT
Y = fft(voltage_signal);

% Compute single-sided spectrum
P2 = abs(Y/N);                    % Two-sided spectrum
P1 = P2(1:floor(N/2)+1);          % Single-sided spectrum
P1(2:end-1) = 2*P1(2:end-1);      % Double amplitude (except DC and Nyquist)

% Frequency vector
f = Fs*(0:floor(N/2))/N;          % Frequency in Hz
f_MHz = f / 1e6;                   % Convert to MHz

% Convert magnitude to dB
magnitude_dB = 20*log10(P1);

% Normalize to 0 dB (optional)
magnitude_dB_normalized = magnitude_dB - max(magnitude_dB);

%% ============== PLOTTING ==============
figure('Position', [100, 100, 1200, 800]);

% Plot 1: Original time-domain signal
subplot(2,2,1);
plot(t*1e6, voltage_signal, 'b', 'LineWidth', 1);
xlabel('Time (\mus)');
ylabel('Voltage (V)');
title('Time Domain: Voltage vs Time');
grid on;
xlim([0, duration*1e6]);

% Plot 2: Frequency spectrum (linear scale)
subplot(2,2,2);
plot(f_MHz, P1, 'r', 'LineWidth', 1);
xlabel('Frequency (MHz)');
ylabel('Magnitude (V)');
title('Frequency Domain: Magnitude vs Frequency');
grid on;
xlim([0, Fs/2/1e6]);

% Plot 3: Frequency spectrum (dB scale)
subplot(2,2,3);
plot(f_MHz, magnitude_dB, 'g', 'LineWidth', 1);
xlabel('Frequency (MHz)');
ylabel('Magnitude (dB)');
title('Frequency Domain: Magnitude (dB) vs Frequency');
grid on;
xlim([0, Fs/2/1e6]);

% Plot 4: Normalized dB spectrum (zoomed)
subplot(2,2,4);
plot(f_MHz, magnitude_dB_normalized, 'm', 'LineWidth', 1);
xlabel('Frequency (MHz)');
ylabel('Magnitude (dB) - Normalized');
title('Normalized Spectrum (0 dB reference)');
grid on;
xlim([0, 20]);  % Zoom to 0-20 MHz
ylim([-60, 5]); % Typical dynamic range
hold on;
yline(-6, '--k', '-6 dB');
yline(-20, '--k', '-20 dB');

sgtitle('Ultrasound Signal Analysis: Time to Frequency Domain Conversion');

%% ============== DISPLAY RESULTS ==============
[peak_magnitude, peak_idx] = max(P1);
peak_frequency = f_MHz(peak_idx);

fprintf('\n========== ANALYSIS RESULTS ==========\n');
fprintf('Sampling Frequency: %.2f MHz\n', Fs/1e6);
fprintf('Signal Duration: %.2f µs\n', duration*1e6);
fprintf('Number of Samples: %d\n', N);
fprintf('Frequency Resolution: %.4f MHz\n', (f(2)-f(1))/1e6);
fprintf('Peak Frequency: %.4f MHz\n', peak_frequency);
fprintf('Peak Magnitude: %.4f V (%.2f dB)\n', peak_magnitude, magnitude_dB(peak_idx));
fprintf('======================================\n');
```

